This is the climax of the campaign.

Do not create an ordinary empty boss arena.

Create a massive zombie gladiator arena inspired by ancient amphitheaters and dark horror architecture.

The environment must communicate that the King rules over the infected.

### 6.1 Arena Architecture

Create a large circular arena.

Include:
- Circular combat floor.
- Massive damaged spectator stands.
- Multiple levels of seating.
- Broken stone structures.
- Destroyed pillars.
- Hanging chains.
- Large metal gates.
- Fire sources around the arena.
- Dark environmental fog.
- Blood-covered stone.
- Damaged arena walls.
- Environmental debris.
- Red accent lighting.

The arena must feel ancient, brutal, and disturbing.

Create an identifiable central combat area.

### 6.2 Zombie Audience — THE HORDE

The spectator stands must contain a massive crowd of zombies.

The intended visual impression is thousands of infected creatures watching the arena.

These zombies are spectators during the boss introduction and Phase 1.

They should:
- Stand in groups.
- Raise their arms.
- Jump.
- Scream.
- Roar.
- Move their bodies.
- React to the boss.
- React to major combat events.

Some spectators may have:
- Missing limbs.
- Exposed rib cages.
- Distorted faces.
- Abnormal body proportions.
- Different zombie silhouettes.

